+            "type": "test",
+            "ref": "tests/test_f30.py::test_ac_1"
+          }
+        },
+        {
+          "id": "AC-2",
+          "text": "Events are written as they happen. A test with a fake SDK stream asserts a `tool_call` line is on disk before the stream yields its `ResultMessage`.",
+          "check": {
+            "type": "test",
+            "ref": "tests/test_f30.py::test_ac_2"
+          }
+        },
+        {
+          "id": "AC-3",
+          "text": "Gate events carry evidence on pass and on fail: each L0 check, each L1 red/green proof and each L2 finding is one `gate_check` with a note saying what was looked at (one test per layer, both outcomes).",
+          "check": {
+            "type": "test",
+            "ref": "tests/test_f30.py::test_ac_3"
+          }
+        },
+        {
+          "id": "AC-4",
+          "text": "Secrets never reach the trace. Args and result snippets are length-capped, and the seat token value plus credential-shaped strings (the F-25 patterns) are replaced with `[redacted]` before the line is written. A test runs a fake tool call whose output contains the seat token and asserts the token appears nowhere in the file.",
+          "check": {
+            "type": "test",
+            "ref": "tests/test_f30.py::test_ac_4"
+          }
+        },
+        {
+          "id": "AC-5",
+          "text": "Tracing never changes a run. A trace write that fails (disk full, permission) is reported once and the run continues; a test makes every write raise and asserts the attempt record is identical to an untraced run.",
+          "check": {
+            "type": "test",
+            "ref": "tests/test_f30.py::test_ac_5"
+          }
+        },
+        {
+          "id": "AC-6",
+          "text": "`factory trace <run-id> [--follow]` prints the trace in order, one line per event; `--follow` keeps printing new events until the attempt ends (published, failed or aborted). It reads only.",
